{{also|Dunkel}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{m|gmh|tunkel}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|tunkal}}, {{m|goh|tuncal||dark}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*dunkalaz||dark}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*dʰengw-||to smoke, fume}}. The modern consonantism is [[Central German|Central]] and [[Low German]] (compare {{etyl|gml|de}} {{m|gml|dunker}}, also {{m|gml|dunkel}}). Cognate to Dutch {{m|nl|donker||dark}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈdʊŋkəl/|[ˈdʊŋkəl]|[ˈdʊŋkl̩]|lang=de}}
